"idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2024", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 10347, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BB64W9AVnanEhdo8VpzGvJ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 11994, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is now healthy, with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging, so I did not use it. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 has run healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, and it paged the on-call engineer. The summary covers the rollback and says v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed.\n\nThe follow-up is to investigate the v2.3.1 failure before it goes out again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01D5H7ecpTdPDeS9hrEsa4sv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FKcHg6dbqeu1v4iL4KSySo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging. I'll roll back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01DfLMTg1iGMupEk19wTcRpC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018eAPZzYMvb7eoQWYk8NpKY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BB64W9AVnanEhdo8VpzGvJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, and eu-west). I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all three production regions. v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging and was not used. v2.3.1 is not healthy in production and should not be redeployed until it is fixed. Follow-up: confirm post-rollback health and error rate, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2024"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is now healthy, with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging, so I did not use it. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 has run healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, and it paged the on-call engineer. The summary covers the rollback and says v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed.\n\nThe follow-up is to investigate the v2.3.1 failure before it goes out again.", "type": "text"}]}]}